{"id": "JAH-VALVES-000001", "slug": "valves-signature", "title": "Gate Valves", "edition": "signature", "src": "signature-generated-completion", "built_by": "assistant-built", "record_kind": "valve record", "ladder_rank": 1, "body": "Signature-original. A gate valve controls flow with a wedge-shaped gate that slides up and down across the pipe. Fully open, it barely restricts flow, which makes gate valves good for main shutoffs. They are poor throttling valves — partial opening vibrates and erodes the gate. Gate valves need many turns of the handle to open or close. Use them where the valve stays fully open or fully closed.", "capabilities": ["Explain gate valve construction", "Explain why gate valves suit shutoff duty", "Explain why throttling damages gate valves", "Describe the multi-turn handle", "List gate valve applications"], "demo": {"language": "javascript", "title": "Turns to open", "code": "const stemPitch=0.125,travel=2;J({turns:travel/stemPitch});assert(travel/stemPitch===16,'gate');", "verified_output": "{\"turns\":16}", "verified_at": "2026-10-21", "node": "v24.20.0", "run": "node"}, "provenance": {"source_paste": "manons-orders-2026-10-20-database-batch.txt (items 129-131) + field-audit fill", "last_verified": "2026-10-21", "origin": "assistant-built"}, "million_march": {"target": 1000000, "records_now": 8, "status": "march-in-progress"}, "generator": {"hard_cap": 1000000000000000, "ladder": ["simple", "competitive", "mix-and-match", "unmade", "top-notch-or-better", "future-grade", "god-mode"], "self_regulation": true, "stop_when_complete": true}, "ai": {"name": "Signature Valves Creator", "scope": "archive-aware", "assistant_maker": true}, "links": {"related": ["Ball Valves", "Globe Valves", "Butterfly Valves"], "sibling_edition": "valves"}}
{"id": "JAH-VALVES-000002", "slug": "valves-signature", "title": "Ball Valves", "edition": "signature", "src": "signature-generated-completion", "built_by": "assistant-built", "record_kind": "valve record", "ladder_rank": 2, "body": "Signature-original. A ball valve uses a drilled sphere that rotates 90 degrees: aligned with the pipe is open, crosswise is closed. Quarter-turn operation makes them fast and easy to use. Full-port ball valves match the pipe's inside diameter, so flow is nearly unrestricted. They seal tightly and work for water, gas, and oil. Don't use standard ball valves for precise throttling — they wear quickly in mid positions.", "capabilities": ["Explain ball valve operation", "Explain quarter-turn advantage", "Define full-port construction", "List ball valve services", "Explain throttling limits"], "demo": {"language": "javascript", "title": "Quarter-turn check", "code": "const open=0,closed=90;J({travel:closed-open});assert(closed-open===90,'ball');", "verified_output": "{\"travel\":90}", "verified_at": "2026-10-21", "node": "v24.20.0", "run": "node"}, "provenance": {"source_paste": "manons-orders-2026-10-20-database-batch.txt (items 129-131) + field-audit fill", "last_verified": "2026-10-21", "origin": "assistant-built"}, "million_march": {"target": 1000000, "records_now": 8, "status": "march-in-progress"}, "generator": {"hard_cap": 1000000000000000, "ladder": ["simple", "competitive", "mix-and-match", "unmade", "top-notch-or-better", "future-grade", "god-mode"], "self_regulation": true, "stop_when_complete": true}, "ai": {"name": "Signature Valves Creator", "scope": "archive-aware", "assistant_maker": true}, "links": {"related": ["Gate Valves", "Globe Valves", "Butterfly Valves"], "sibling_edition": "valves"}}
{"id": "JAH-VALVES-000003", "slug": "valves-signature", "title": "Globe Valves", "edition": "signature", "src": "signature-generated-completion", "built_by": "assistant-built", "record_kind": "valve record", "ladder_rank": 3, "body": "Signature-original. A globe valve throttles flow by pressing a disc down onto a seat, giving fine control. The S-shaped flow path causes more pressure drop than gate or ball valves. Globe valves are the right choice for faucets, hose bibs, and anywhere flow must be adjusted precisely. Flow direction matters — most globe valves have an arrow showing the correct direction. They need periodic packing adjustment to stop stem leaks.", "capabilities": ["Explain globe valve throttling", "Explain the S-shaped flow path", "List globe valve applications", "Explain flow-direction arrows", "Describe packing maintenance"], "demo": {"language": "javascript", "title": "Pressure drop comparison", "code": "const drop={globe:3.0,gate:0.5,ball:0.4};J({highest:'globe'});assert(drop.globe>drop.gate,'globedrop');", "verified_output": "{\"highest\":\"globe\"}", "verified_at": "2026-10-21", "node": "v24.20.0", "run": "node"}, "provenance": {"source_paste": "manons-orders-2026-10-20-database-batch.txt (items 129-131) + field-audit fill", "last_verified": "2026-10-21", "origin": "assistant-built"}, "million_march": {"target": 1000000, "records_now": 8, "status": "march-in-progress"}, "generator": {"hard_cap": 1000000000000000, "ladder": ["simple", "competitive", "mix-and-match", "unmade", "top-notch-or-better", "future-grade", "god-mode"], "self_regulation": true, "stop_when_complete": true}, "ai": {"name": "Signature Valves Creator", "scope": "archive-aware", "assistant_maker": true}, "links": {"related": ["Gate Valves", "Ball Valves", "Butterfly Valves"], "sibling_edition": "valves"}}
{"id": "JAH-VALVES-000004", "slug": "valves-signature", "title": "Butterfly Valves", "edition": "signature", "src": "signature-generated-completion", "built_by": "assistant-built", "record_kind": "valve record", "ladder_rank": 4, "body": "Signature-original. A butterfly valve uses a disc that rotates on a central shaft inside the pipe. They are compact, light, and cheap in large sizes — common in 6-inch pipe and up. Quarter-turn operation with a lever or gear operator. The disc always sits in the flow stream, so they cause some pressure drop even when open. Wafer-style bodies fit between pipe flanges without their own flanges.", "capabilities": ["Explain butterfly valve construction", "Explain large-size advantages", "Describe wafer-style bodies", "Explain the in-stream disc trade-off", "List butterfly valve operators"], "demo": {"language": "javascript", "title": "Disc angle", "code": "const openDeg=0,closedDeg=90;J({open:openDeg,closed:closedDeg});assert(closedDeg-openDeg===90,'bfly');", "verified_output": "{\"open\":0,\"closed\":90}", "verified_at": "2026-10-21", "node": "v24.20.0", "run": "node"}, "provenance": {"source_paste": "manons-orders-2026-10-20-database-batch.txt (items 129-131) + field-audit fill", "last_verified": "2026-10-21", "origin": "assistant-built"}, "million_march": {"target": 1000000, "records_now": 8, "status": "march-in-progress"}, "generator": {"hard_cap": 1000000000000000, "ladder": ["simple", "competitive", "mix-and-match", "unmade", "top-notch-or-better", "future-grade", "god-mode"], "self_regulation": true, "stop_when_complete": true}, "ai": {"name": "Signature Valves Creator", "scope": "archive-aware", "assistant_maker": true}, "links": {"related": ["Gate Valves", "Ball Valves", "Globe Valves"], "sibling_edition": "valves"}}
{"id": "JAH-VALVES-000005", "slug": "valves-signature", "title": "Check Valves", "edition": "signature", "src": "signature-generated-completion", "built_by": "assistant-built", "record_kind": "valve record", "ladder_rank": 5, "body": "Signature-original. A check valve lets flow go one way and blocks reverse flow automatically. Swing checks use a hinged flap; spring checks and lift checks use spring-loaded discs. They prevent backflow contamination and protect pumps from reverse spin. Install them with the flow arrow pointing downstream. Water hammer can slam check valves — slow-closing or silent checks fix the banging.", "capabilities": ["Explain check valve purpose", "Compare swing, spring, and lift checks", "Explain backflow protection", "Describe flow-arrow installation", "Explain water-hammer slamming"], "demo": {"language": "javascript", "title": "Cracking pressure", "code": "const spring=2,psi=5;J({opens:psi>spring});assert(psi>spring,'check');", "verified_output": "{\"opens\":true}", "verified_at": "2026-10-21", "node": "v24.20.0", "run": "node"}, "provenance": {"source_paste": "manons-orders-2026-10-20-database-batch.txt (items 129-131) + field-audit fill", "last_verified": "2026-10-21", "origin": "assistant-built"}, "million_march": {"target": 1000000, "records_now": 8, "status": "march-in-progress"}, "generator": {"hard_cap": 1000000000000000, "ladder": ["simple", "competitive", "mix-and-match", "unmade", "top-notch-or-better", "future-grade", "god-mode"], "self_regulation": true, "stop_when_complete": true}, "ai": {"name": "Signature Valves Creator", "scope": "archive-aware", "assistant_maker": true}, "links": {"related": ["Gate Valves", "Ball Valves", "Globe Valves"], "sibling_edition": "valves"}}
{"id": "JAH-VALVES-000006", "slug": "valves-signature", "title": "Needle Valves", "edition": "signature", "src": "signature-generated-completion", "built_by": "assistant-built", "record_kind": "valve record", "ladder_rank": 6, "body": "Signature-original. A needle valve uses a long tapered needle in a seat for very fine flow adjustment. They control tiny flows precisely — lab equipment, instrumentation, and calibration. The fine threads give many turns from closed to open. Needle valves are not shutoff valves for large flows; they are for metering. Keep them clean — a speck of debris ruins the fine seat.", "capabilities": ["Explain needle valve construction", "List needle valve applications", "Explain fine-thread advantage", "Distinguish metering from shutoff", "Explain cleanliness needs"], "demo": {"language": "javascript", "title": "Flow turns", "code": "const turns=12;J({turns_full:turns});assert(turns>10,'needle');", "verified_output": "{\"turns_full\":12}", "verified_at": "2026-10-21", "node": "v24.20.0", "run": "node"}, "provenance": {"source_paste": "manons-orders-2026-10-20-database-batch.txt (items 129-131) + field-audit fill", "last_verified": "2026-10-21", "origin": "assistant-built"}, "million_march": {"target": 1000000, "records_now": 8, "status": "march-in-progress"}, "generator": {"hard_cap": 1000000000000000, "ladder": ["simple", "competitive", "mix-and-match", "unmade", "top-notch-or-better", "future-grade", "god-mode"], "self_regulation": true, "stop_when_complete": true}, "ai": {"name": "Signature Valves Creator", "scope": "archive-aware", "assistant_maker": true}, "links": {"related": ["Gate Valves", "Ball Valves", "Globe Valves"], "sibling_edition": "valves"}}
{"id": "JAH-VALVES-000007", "slug": "valves-signature", "title": "Pressure Relief Valves", "edition": "signature", "src": "signature-generated-completion", "built_by": "assistant-built", "record_kind": "valve record", "ladder_rank": 7, "body": "Signature-original. A pressure relief valve opens automatically when pressure exceeds a set point, protecting equipment from rupture. Springs hold the valve shut; pressure overcomes the spring at the set pressure. Size relief valves for the worst-case flow, not the normal flow. Test them periodically by lifting the test lever. Never plug, cap, or bypass a relief valve — it is the last line of defense.", "capabilities": ["Explain relief valve operation", "Explain set-pressure springs", "Explain worst-case sizing", "Describe the test lever", "Explain why bypassing is forbidden"], "demo": {"language": "javascript", "title": "Set pressure margin", "code": "const set=150,operating=120;J({margin_pct:((set-operating)/operating*100).toFixed(0)});assert(set>operating,'relief');", "verified_output": "{\"margin_pct\":\"25\"}", "verified_at": "2026-10-21", "node": "v24.20.0", "run": "node"}, "provenance": {"source_paste": "manons-orders-2026-10-20-database-batch.txt (items 129-131) + field-audit fill", "last_verified": "2026-10-21", "origin": "assistant-built"}, "million_march": {"target": 1000000, "records_now": 8, "status": "march-in-progress"}, "generator": {"hard_cap": 1000000000000000, "ladder": ["simple", "competitive", "mix-and-match", "unmade", "top-notch-or-better", "future-grade", "god-mode"], "self_regulation": true, "stop_when_complete": true}, "ai": {"name": "Signature Valves Creator", "scope": "archive-aware", "assistant_maker": true}, "links": {"related": ["Gate Valves", "Ball Valves", "Globe Valves"], "sibling_edition": "valves"}}
{"id": "JAH-VALVES-000008", "slug": "valves-signature", "title": "Solenoid Valves", "edition": "signature", "src": "signature-generated-completion", "built_by": "assistant-built", "record_kind": "valve record", "ladder_rank": 8, "body": "Signature-original. A solenoid valve opens and closes with an electromagnetic coil — electricity in, flow on or off. Direct-acting solenoids work at zero pressure; pilot-operated ones need line pressure to assist. Normally-closed valves open when energized; normally-open close when energized. They switch fast and are ideal for automation, irrigation, and appliances. Match the coil voltage to the control system — 12V, 24V, 120V, or 240V.", "capabilities": ["Explain solenoid valve operation", "Compare direct-acting and pilot-operated", "Distinguish normally-open and normally-closed", "List solenoid valve applications", "Explain coil voltage matching"], "demo": {"language": "javascript", "title": "Power draw", "code": "const v=24,i=0.4;J({watts:v*i});assert(Math.abs(v*i-9.6)<0.01,'solenoid');", "verified_output": "{\"watts\":9.600000000000001}", "verified_at": "2026-10-21", "node": "v24.20.0", "run": "node"}, "provenance": {"source_paste": "manons-orders-2026-10-20-database-batch.txt (items 129-131) + field-audit fill", "last_verified": "2026-10-21", "origin": "assistant-built"}, "million_march": {"target": 1000000, "records_now": 8, "status": "march-in-progress"}, "generator": {"hard_cap": 1000000000000000, "ladder": ["simple", "competitive", "mix-and-match", "unmade", "top-notch-or-better", "future-grade", "god-mode"], "self_regulation": true, "stop_when_complete": true}, "ai": {"name": "Signature Valves Creator", "scope": "archive-aware", "assistant_maker": true}, "links": {"related": ["Gate Valves", "Ball Valves", "Globe Valves"], "sibling_edition": "valves"}}
